   "title": "A sharp E-W step in the radar north of Urama and Morón",
   "text": "At about 10.51-10.52°N, from 68.45°W east to Morón, NISAR's motion jumps by up to about 30 cm over 1.5-2 km, with a thin low-coherence seam. Copernicus EMS's Sentinel-1 map shows a step of the same size here (its sign convention is not resolved). GEER found no surface rupture in the field in this area.",
